     ('Heat budget, temperature and albedo', [(M['heat'], M['p2']), (Q2[3], M['inv'])], UND[1], 'Four ways heat moves: <b>Touch · Lift · Slide · Beam</b> = Conduction, Convection, Advection, Radiation (the only one that needs no medium). Surplus inside 40° N/S, deficit beyond. Sun’s short waves come in, Earth’s long waves go out; snow and ice have high albedo.'),
     ('Temperature inversion', [(M['inv'], M['pres'])], UND[2], 'Inversion needs <b>CALM</b>: Clear sky · Absence of mixing · Long nights · Mountain valleys. The warm lid traps smoke and fog (pollution dome) but can spare frost-prone crops.'),
     ('Air pressure, pressure belts and winds', [(M['pres'], M['p5']), (Q5[0], Q5[1]), (Q11[1], Q11[2])], UND[3], '<b>Coriolis: zero at the Equator, maximum at the Poles; Right in the North, Left in the South.</b> The pressure gradient sets speed and direction; friction slows the wind. Seven belts: 3 thermal + 4 dynamic, following the overhead Sun.'),
     ('Geostrophic winds and jet streams', [(M['geo'], M['loc']), (Q5[1], Q5[2]), (jet, jet + 1)], UND[4], '<b>Geostrophic = along the isobars</b> (pressure push balances Coriolis, no friction). Jet streams sit at 8-15 km: <b>polar 50-60°</b> (strong in winter), <b>subtropical 20-30°</b>. Warming weakens and meanders them; the subtropical westerly jet drags Western Disturbances into India.'),
     ('Local winds and monsoonal winds', [(M['loc'], M['hum']), (Q11[0], Q11[1])], UND[5], '<b>Chinook</b> = snow-eater (warm, dry, descending). <b>Loo</b> = North India’s hot May-June wind. <b>Harmattan</b> = West Africa’s dry “doctor wind”. Cold ones: <b>Bora, Mistral, Purga, Pampero</b>. Monsoon = seasonal reversal of winds.'),
     ('Humidity, condensation, clouds and storms', [(M['hum'], M['p11']), (Q11[2], Q11[4]), (Q11[5], Q11[6])], UND[6], '<b>Cloud levels: above 6,000 m high (cirrus, ice) · 2,000-6,000 m mid (alto) · below 2,000 m low</b>; cumulonimbus climbs through all levels. Dew forms when the surface falls below the dew point, so a cloudy night (a blanket) gives no dew.'),
     ('Air masses and fronts', [(M['air'], M['cyc'])], UND[7], '<b>COWS</b> = the four fronts: Cold, Occluded, Warm, Stationary. Cold front: fast, cumulonimbus, thunder, hail. Warm front: slow, stratus, steady drizzle. Air-mass codes: <b>m</b> = moist sea, <b>c</b> = dry land; T = warm, P = cold.'),
     ('Cyclones', [(M['cyc'], M['p14']), (eye, eye + 1), (M['p14'], M['kop'])], UND[8], '<b>Tropical = Thermal engine</b> (warm sea of at least 26.5 °C, no fronts, 10-30°, heavy rain for a few hours). <b>Temperate = Dynamic</b> (born on fronts, 30-60°, rain for days). Both spin counter-clockwise in the north, clockwise in the south.'),
